sam: Heads-up — customer is hitting intermittent 504s when using the Go SDK. They report the SDK retry wrapper keeps firing after the request context is canceled which doubles downstream effects. Repro below, looking for quick triage.

sam: Repro (customer code simplified):
```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 2*time.Second)
defer cancel()
client := &http.Client{
  Timeout: 10 * time.Second,
  Transport: &http.Transport{
    MaxIdleConnsPerHost: 10,
  },
}
req, _ := http.NewRequest("POST", "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate", bytes.NewReader(b))
req = req.WithContext(ctx)
resp, err := client.Do(req) // wrapped by sdk.Retry.Do(ctx, fn)
```

sam: Logs from customer (trimmed):
```
2026-03-16T10:12:34Z ERR request canceled while waiting for connection
2026-03-16T10:12:36Z INFO retry attempt=2 calling backend
2026-03-16T10:12:37Z ERR upstream 504 Gateway Timeout
```

anya: Can you paste the SDK call site? is the retry wrapper using the request's ctx for each attempt or ignoring it? Also which Go version?

sam: Go 1.20, SDK v0.9.1. Wrapper looks like:
```go
func (r *Retryer) Do(ctx context.Context, fn func() (*http.Response, error)) (*http.Response, error) {
  for i:=0;i<r.max;i++{
    res, err := fn()
    if err==nil { return res, nil }
    time.Sleep(r.backoff(i)) // <-- this sleep is not ctx-aware
  }
  return nil, errors.New("max retries")
}
```

support-evan: Ah — two obvious smells: 1) using both client.Timeout and ctx timeout can interact weirdly, 2) the retry backoff isn't selecting on ctx.Done(), so cancel won't break sleeps. Also check Transport.ResponseHeaderTimeout and DialContext. Recommend: remove client.Timeout (use ctx), set Transport.ResponseHeaderTimeout = 5s, and make backoff ctx-aware.

eng-ryan: Confirmed — I reproduced locally. The SDK's retry loop calls fn() which does req.WithContext(ctx) the first time, but subsequent attempts reconstruct the request without re-attaching the original ctx (we clone the *http.Request incorrectly). Also our backoff is uninterruptible. Two bug items: request context propagation and interruptible backoff.

eng-ryan: Minimal fix sketch:
```go
// in retry loop
for i:=0;i<max;i++{
  select{
  case <-ctx.Done():
    return nil, ctx.Err()
  default:
  }
  // create request for attempt, but use req = req.WithContext(ctx) every time
  res, err := fnWithCtx(ctx)
  if err==nil { return res, nil }
  // interruptible sleep
  timer := time.NewTimer(backoff(i))
  select{ case <-timer.C: case <-ctx.Done(): timer.Stop(); return nil, ctx.Err() }
}
```

sam: Customer also reported increased billing because the backend saw retries hitting model tokens multiple times. They want a hotfix.

infra-bot: Incident checklist created: INC-2026-73. Please attach repro binary / unit test.

anya: Can you add a unit test that cancels the context while sleeping and asserts fn is not called again? If yes we can cut a patch.

eng-ryan: Will open PR with two changes: 1) ensure Request.WithContext used on every attempt, 2) make backoff ctx-selectable. I'll include a unit test and a small note to ops about possible customer billing impact.

sam: Thanks — marking customer as escalated, +cc @support-evan for billing outreach. :exclamation:
